🚽 Test case: #193 -- a by-value struct/union member-access sub-expression
🚽 (`bussin b.corner;`) can be returned, symmetric with the argument side.
🚽 The member's blob is copied into a fresh heap allocation before the
🚽 function's scope (where `b` lives) is torn down, then copied into the
🚽 caller's destination -- so the returned value is independent of the
🚽 (now-gone) source.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Box {
    gang Point corner;
};

gang Point get_corner(gang Box b) {
    bussin b.corner;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Box b;
    b.corner.x = 11;
    b.corner.y = 22;
    gang Point c = get_corner(b);
    yapping("%d %d", c.x, c.y);
}
